#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# neville_theta_c

#% text
# `neville_theta_c(z, m)` gives the Neville theta function `theta_c(z | m)`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `theta_c(z | m)` is `theta_2(pi*z/(2*K(m)), q)/theta_2(0, q)`, with the nome `q` of `m` (DLMF 20.1, 22.2). It is even in `z` and `theta_c(0 | m)` is 1.

#% item
# `jacobi_cn(z, m)` is `theta_c/theta_n`.

#% item
# Machine numbers and balls give numerical values.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
neville_theta_c(0.5, 0.3)
#% output
#= 0.8964776434470245

#% cell
neville_theta_c(0, 0.3)
#% output
#= 1

#% cell
neville_theta_c(1.0, 0.9)
#% output
#= 0.7993416994774856

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The quotient that gives `cn`:

#% cell
neville_theta_c(0.7, 0.4)/neville_theta_n(0.7, 0.4) - jacobi_cn(0.7, 0.4)
#% output
#= 0.0

